schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-vegalite-01-canonical-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-vegalite
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: canonical-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook data visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.VegaLite. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Use deterministic local data and explicit VegaLite encodings.
  text: |-
    Create a canonical Kino.VegaLite Livebook cell. Install kino_vega_lite, vega_lite, and kino, alias VegaLite as Vl, build deterministic local rows as maps, create a VegaLite spec with Vl.new, Vl.data_from_values, Vl.mark, and Vl.encode_field, and render it directly or wrap it with Kino.VegaLite.new/1 when streaming is required. Include at least one bar, line, scatter, or heatmap chart with tooltips and clear axis titles.

    Requirements: document Livebook/Kino compatibility and that this is not a Jupyter ipywidgets chart; describe the data fields and Vega-Lite types; include explicit type: options on every encode_field; include accessible colors, labels, tooltip fields, fallback local data, and safe execution checks that avoid remote data by default, credentials, eval, shell calls, giant inline datasets, and pushing to a bare VegaLite spec.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-vegalite-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_vega_lite, vega_lite, and kino, aliases VegaLite as Vl, and uses VegaLite plus Kino.VegaLite APIs."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino runtime and distinguish it from Jupyter widgets."
  - "Reactive state: streaming or push behavior uses a Kino.VegaLite widget, not a bare VegaLite spec."
  - "Data shape: local rows, field names, field types, tooltip fields, and Vega-Lite encodings are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: chart title, axes, tooltips, readable colors, and fallback local data are present."
  - "Safe execution: no remote data by default, credentials, eval, shell commands, giant inline datasets, or push calls on a bare spec."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid Elixir and every encode_field call includes an explicit type."
    - "The cell uses supported VegaLite and Kino.VegaLite functions."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements a canonical declarative chart with deterministic data, encodings, labels, and tooltips."
    - "Uses Kino.VegaLite-specific rules for static specs versus streamable widgets."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "The chart type matches the data and is easy to read in a notebook cell."
    - "Axes, legends, tooltips, and colors support accessible interpretation."
    - "The output has stable sizing and clear fallback behavior."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles empty rows, missing fields, wrong temporal types, duplicate categories, and extreme values."
    - "Uses deterministic bounded data."
    - "Documents when to aggregate, sample, or use data_from_url for larger data."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.VegaLite-centered and preserves declarative Vega-Lite semantics."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-vegalite
- canonical-widget

